.TH gen_config 3 "05/12/95" "CADC"
.nh
.SH NAME
gen_config, config_close, config_get, config_open \- operations on 
configuration library files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.LP
.nf
.ft B
#include "gen_types.h"
#include "gen_config.h"
.ft
.fi
.LP
.nf
.ta 0.8i
.ft B
void	config_close()
.ft
.fi
.LP
.nf
.ft B
int	config_get( key, fn )
char	\(**key;
pfb	fn
.ft
.fi
.LP
.nf
.ft B
int	config_open( rootname, config_file )
char	\(**rootname;
char	\(**\(**config_file;

.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B config_close(\|)
closes the configuration library.
.LP
.B config_get(\|)
applys the config function
.I fn 
to every line in the config file with keyword \(eq
.IR key.
This function returns GC_SUCCESS upon normal completion, or 
GC_E_KEY_NOT_FOUND if the key could not be found.
.LP
.B config_open(\|)
Initializes the configuration file. The 
.I rootname 
is used to calculate the config file name. The
.I config_file
is returned from the function and is the name and full path of 
the config file opened.
The function returns GC_SUCCESS upon normal completion,
GC_E_MEMORY if memory allocation failed, or GC_E_FILE_NOT_FOUND
if the file could not be found.
The config file is located by the environement variable
APPNAME_CONFIG_DIR directory, where
.I APPNAME
is the name of the application for which the config file
is required. If environment variable APPNAME_CONFIG_DIR is not set,
then the directory defined by environment variable DEFAULT_CONFIG_DIR
is searched. Finally, if the config file is not located from either
of these two environment variables, the current directory is searched.

.SH AUTHOR
